{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration","id":342244,"title":"Prototype as Lunar Inspiration...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-16T14:24:36-08:00","id":342244,"title":"Prototype as Lunar Inspiration...","content":"...Why don't people like it?<br /> <br /> Let's look, not at the cancerous viral body horror, but at the mechanics of how the powers of these characters work.<br /> <br /> They have superhuman strength,m and speed, and toughness, and endurance, and regeneration. They can take the shapes of creatures by eating them, and also absorb their memeories and perfectly imitate their mannerisms. In combat, they use the natural weapons of creatures they've devoured. Preferred methods of learning information about the conspiracy? Hunt down people who know, eat them,and absorb their memories. James Heller himself has the power to easily track down anycreature who he declares his prey, and can sense when it's an apropriate time to go in for the kill.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Absorbing memories from creatures in your hearts blood library is something being mentioned as examples of Lunar mental attribute charms.<br /> <br /> James Heller, from the sequel, works even better as a Lunar. His Xp goes into a level system, and once he gets enough he doesn't get new powers, he gets more super strength, better regen, or can jump higher.<br /> <br /> New Natural Weapons and such powers? He has to go out, hunt down a creature with that power or natural weapon, and eat it. IF he wants better claws, he has to find something with stronger or slightly different claws, or maybe on other attribute that matches well with claws, and eat that.<br /> <br /> James isn't like Alex. He's the same person before and after infection.<br /> <br /> He gaind his powers, becuase, after his family was killed by the infected, he decided he was going wipe out the infection and Alex Mercer or die trying, and if he died he was taking as many of those fuckers with him as possible.<br /> <br /> He proves to stubborn to die, as in the prologue of his game, he fights off or escapes from some of the more advnaced infected creatures, survives a tank explosion, and attacked Alex Mercer himself. He gets infected for his troubles, and h survives that too, and that's how he gets his powers.<br /> <br /> Isn't surviving a fuck ton of bad stuff, physical danger, life altering crises, and and emotional turmoil supposed to be how Lunars are judged worthy of their powers?<br /> <br /> So I'm confused. I look at it and I see the parallels, but people seem to be shutting it down based solely on Aesthetics or the protagonists being &quot;shoggoths&quot; or &quot;rubbermen&quot; when they're not.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T14:37:23-08:00","id":342292,"title":"","content":"I think the main problem is actually that Heller and Mercer aren't particularly tied into the other Lunar themes of shamanism, primal forces, and adaptability. You can pull some cool combat tricks off them on occasion, but then most of those tricks were easy to come up with already. Claws, super-strength, regeneration, speed, and so on are things Lunars already do. What more can be pulled from Prototype that hasn't already been realized? Mostly &quot;shoggoth&quot; type powers, like lashing out with flesh tentacles, devouring people instantly, or reforming from a drop of blood.<br /> <br /> To use them as inspiration for new Lunar powers, they'd need to offer up something that Lunars don't currently have but that they should possess. A Lunar really shouldn't be shapeshifting his arm into a sword or a whipfist, he should be manifesting Claws of the Silver Moon or drawing his moonsilver grimcleaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T14:53:10-08:00","id":342304,"title":"","content":"I haven't really seen anyone hate on prototype for lunar inspiration? I think that the &quot;feel&quot; of prototype is very different from the &quot;feel&quot; of lunars. Lunars got the whole &quot;Defender&quot; theme going and little in prototype feels like defending anything. Prototype is about killing as many people as viscerally as possible, and while the game's story may say otherwise the gameplay says so and only so. (I realize this is a less well phrased argument for what, kyeudo was saying... Sowwy)<br /> <br /> I could totally see myself using Prototype as inspiration for chimeras, though. Devastating powers wielded by monsters who were once human, and reality defying biology acting as a weapons against anyone and anything; sounds like a match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:08:12-08:00","id":342316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342292#post342292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main problem is actually that Heller and Mercer aren't particularly tied into the other Lunar themes of shamanism, primal forces, and adaptability. You can pull some cool combat tricks off them on occasion, but then most of those tricks were easy to come up with already. Claws, super-strength, regeneration, speed, and so on are things Lunars already do. What more can be pulled from Prototype that hasn't already been realized? Mostly &quot;shoggoth&quot; type powers, like lashing out with flesh tentacles, devouring people instantly, or reforming from a drop of blood.<br /> <br /> To use them as inspiration for new Lunar powers, they'd need to offer up something that Lunars don't currently have but that they should possess. A Lunar really shouldn't be shapeshifting his arm into a sword or a whipfist, he should be manifesting Claws of the Silver Moon or drawing his moonsilver grimcleaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do fit with the Lunar themes of endurance, being an outsider, monstrousness and mutability. I don't think all Lunars need to fit with all of the themes of the Lunars, or that makes the field of Lunar inspiration very thin indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:08:12-08:00","id":342317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration#post342244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's look, not at the cancerous viral body horror, but at the mechanics of how the powers of these characters work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, you <i>absolutely have to look at the cancerous viral body horror</i>. You can't simply divorce the power mechanic from its narrative aesthetic or (meta)physical manifestation and say it fits because the mechanical effect seems close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:13:54-08:00","id":342327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Lunar who uses his Heart's blood as his primary weapon, mixing and matching the natural weapons of those he's devoured to augment his already impressive strength, that should be something that a Lunar can do, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's probably going to look more like Animorphs more than anything from Prototype. Natural weapons are of the claws/fangs/hooves/horns variety for pretty much every monster in existence and one set of claws is pretty much like any other once you get into the world of RPG weapon stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see people talking about how Prototype makes for bad Lunars, but the methods they use just scream lunar. It all seems to be a case of judging it by how it looks than by how it <i>is</i> </div> </div> </div>I think you are missing an important connection here. If the methods used in Prototype are like what Lunars are already doing, then what should Lunars take from Prototype? It sounds like they already have everything important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Also,I could totally see &quot;Regenerate from a drop&quot; as an essence five, stamina five stamina charm at the end of a <b><i>really</i></b> long branch of the stamina tree focused on health and regen. </div> </div> </div>It's never going to happen. The closest things to such immortality for a PC we ever saw was Immortal Malevolence Enslavement and that cost you an Essence dot every time you got brought back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:16:03-08:00","id":342328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342292#post342292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lunar really shouldn't be shapeshifting his arm into a sword or a whipfist, he should be manifesting Claws of the Silver Moon or drawing his moonsilver grimcleaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, kind of? But if you take the Heart's Blood of a demon that naturally has a sword-arm or a whipfist, then you'll get it and be able to use it - by shapeshifting into that creature, or possibly turning your arm into that creature's arm with something like HBR.<br /> <br /> However, that stuff solidly belongs in the SHAPESHIFTING/FORM-STEALING slot of the Lunar toolkit, not the ATTRIBUTE CHARMS THAT REFLECT YOUR NORMAL HUMAN CAPABILITIES slot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342292#post342292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main problem is actually that Heller and Mercer aren't particularly tied into the other Lunar themes of shamanism, primal forces, and adaptability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also god damn I am so sick of shamanism being cited as a Lunar Thing. Maybe it should be but there have never been actual good examples of it being used in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Lunars can take a lot of visual cues from the aesthetics of the IRL Indigenous shaman but they have never, ever been described as interacting with spirits the way shamans IRL do.<br /> <br /> When all of your &quot;mortal&quot; spirit interaction for 2 editions is divided into &quot;groveling,&quot; &quot;organized religion somewhat evocative of Christianity, with priest as intercessor&quot; and &quot;thaumaturgy,&quot; and thaumaturgy is presented as MUCH more hermetic (as in, scientifically-oriented) than shamanic (as in, emotionally- or spiritually-oriented), shamanism as I think it's intending to be depicted is not represented on-screen in-setting pretty much ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:54:36-08:00","id":342355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is the point I'm making.<br /> <br /> Lunars are already doing almost everything you can do in those games, so why are those games said to not be Lunary? Saying that those characters and powers are not Lunary tells me that I can't make a character with the Shapeshifting+Super Atributes&quot; tool kit, sprouting the natural weapons of things I ate, absorbing the memories of people I ate and taking their faces to infiltrate places are not going to be a thing I can do as a Lunar PC, and all of that sounds Lunary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because second edition Lunars was ashamed to be associated with werewolves and went out of its way to avoid as much of the source material as possible while cribbing from sources further and further afield from the basic concept. This makes them very much not the sort of thing that Lunars should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:55:02-08:00","id":342356,"title":"","content":"Because Prototype &amp; its ilk are a Science Fiction Action story. Exalted is a Pulp Fantasy story. They intersect in some places, but biology as a property of knowledge isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> That is, generally if a character is tapping into forces beyond themselves, those forces have a mind and will of their own. Mercer / The Thing / etc tend to work of the cold/alien anti-will of biology.<br /> <br /> There may be some places for Mad Science in Exalted (sort of, of a fantasy sort) but the Lunar are the opposite of this.<br /> <br /> Alex Mercer exhibits his powers in an <u><i>Unnatural </i></u>way. Lunars express their powers in a mythic, &quot;<i><u>Hyper-natural&quot;</u> </i>way.<br /> <br /> So the Hydra, Cerberus, Ladon the 100 Headed Dragon, Peng, the Basilisk, the Qilin or Xiezhi or Gramar... there are thousands of combinations, powers, narratives to draw on. All without slumming around in Science Fiction / Resident Evil genere.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars and the characters from Prototype do . . .generally, sort-of the same things, but they do them in completely different ways, for completely different reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T16:33:24-08:00","id":342391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is the point I'm making.<br /> <br /> Lunars are already doing almost everything you can do in those games, so why are those games said to not be Lunary? Saying that those characters and powers are not Lunary tells me that I can't make a character with the Shapeshifting+Super Atributes&quot; tool kit, sprouting the natural weapons of things I ate, absorbing the memories of people I ate and taking their faces to infiltrate places are not going to be a thing I can do as a Lunar PC, and all of that sounds Lunary.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are still getting it backwards. Lunars are the superset, Prototype a subset. The things Mercer does are largely things that Lunars can do or can get done, but that doesn't mean that Mercer is a good example of a Lunar character. Mercer is, in so many ways, limited and lacking compared to a Lunar. A Lunar is just as easily Spiderman or the Incredible Hulk or Red XIII.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T16:58:40-08:00","id":342398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342356#post342356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alex Mercer exhibits his powers in an <u><i>Unnatural </i></u>way. Lunars express their powers in a mythic, &quot;<i><u>Hyper-natural&quot;</u> </i>way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. When I first played the game he felt like an Abyssal to me with a sci-fi &quot;resurrection&quot; to get his revenge and powers that I'd define more as body horror than shapeshifting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T17:13:39-08:00","id":342401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I fly with wings or fly with a spell, I'm still flying.<br /> <br /> The <b>What</b> is what's important, not the <b>How</b> or<b> Why</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Superman is a great source of Lunar inspiration. He can fly, move really fast, punch hard, and take a bunch of damage.<br /> <br /> Oh, and switching from Superman to Clark Kent must be something kinda like shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T17:42:17-08:00","id":342415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other than the bolded part, you're not far off. If Lunar Charms are attribute based, then &quot;Super Strength&quot;, &quot;Super Speed&quot;, and &quot;Incredible Toughness&quot; all fit somewhere into the low level charms of the strength, dexterity, and stamina trees. Flight, niot so much, but if a Lunar doesn't get it from shapeshifting, it is probably something a Lunar could learn to do as a hige level charm or combination of charms.<br /> <br /> The bolded, however, is clearly just a case of overly simplifying an argument in order to make it look silly, and that's no way to make a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this 'super normal attribute&quot; thing is where you cross the line. Superman is very much not Lunar, regardless of his exaggerated physical capabilities, because Lunars don't just use exaggerated physical capabilities. They engage in abnormal adjustments that resemble the traits of other animals. Instead of boring super-toughness, they get rough skin, thick fur and armored scales to resist injury. Their strength increases, way back when, were associated with their muscles looking like they would burst through the skin. Their speed results in odd joint and limb structures that are obviously not human, as does their superior grace. The closest thing that Superman might have to a related concept is having lasers for eyes, supposing you could find a legendary beast that has lasers for eyes.<br /> <br /> The developers of Prototype were under no obligation to map out a great example of a Lunar. They were engaged in making their own narrative, which might have some usable parts if you squint, but ultimately is not close enough a match, especially not when we have Liminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T17:53:29-08:00","id":342419,"title":"","content":"Chiming in with Lunars being more natural than unnatural. One theory as to why dragons exist in myth is that they're a combination of all the primal predators humans faced. The jaws and teeth of a wolf, the needle fangs and coiling sinewous body of a snake, the wicked claws of a great cat or raptor ect. That's what a Lunar is, a lunar uses shapeshifting to become everything that ever made primitive humans seek shelter or hide in the dark. It's ancient and mythic and awesome in every sense of the word. Like when I see a tiger, deep down I know that if it was hungry and had the chance it would hunt me down, kill me and eat me, it's stronger than I am, sharper and bigger teeth and claws. I just get this gut feeling than I am its prey.<br /> <br /> Mercer definitely does exhibit a lot of those traits, the face stealer and adapting to anything. The aesthetics and specifics are off though. Giant scything arms are terrifying but don't evoke thoughts of the natural world, the association isn't there in the same way. He's a monster, not a predator, if that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:11:56-08:00","id":342429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I fly with wings or fly with a spell, I'm still flying.<br /> <br /> The <b>What</b> is what's important, not the <b>How</b> or<b> Why</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is just completely and absolutely wrong. <br /> <br /> After all, all of the things we've been talking about, super-strength, super-speed, flight, impersonation, are also part of the Solar purview. If methods and themes don't matter, then there's really no point in having Lunars (or any other Exalts) at all. Solars can do all the stuff, and do it very well, so why have anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:19:37-08:00","id":342433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is the point I'm making.<br /> <br /> Lunars are already doing almost everything you can do in those games, so why are those games said to not be Lunary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some people seem to be fixated too much on animal themes. Which Prototype doesn't have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:22:01-08:00","id":342439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can't play a character who uses his shapeshifting to augment his already super human attributes with the physical traits of the various creature he hunted down and ate(and his Totemistic Spirit Shape), or a character who can't eat someone, and then use their shape and manerysms to infiltrate an enemy stronghold, then whats the point of playing a Lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can of course do all of this, so it's not a great place to be coming to the conversation from.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that really stops the Prototype boys from being a Lunar story is that Lunars just aren't protean blobs of flesh, the way the Blacklight victims are. They change their forms, certainly but generally from one specific form into another specific form. When a Lunar uses Claws of the Moon it's working to a specific model, not just transforming it's forearms into appearently-metal with an arbitrary number of spikes. <br /> <br /> Of course there is a subset of Lunars who are right into that, and both games make excellent Chimera stories. In fact there are a lot of ways in which both Exalted and Prototype dig into the same symbols and messaging about physical stability and wholeness reflecting mental stability and wholeness ... it's just that Exalted is up-front with it's 'we dont do this because then we gent infested citiies' line, while protoype kind of buries the lede.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:29:09-08:00","id":342454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why the Solar has Melee charms, and brawl charms and not strength charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Solar Charms don't necessarily key of Strentgh as an attribute they have always had Charms for just flat out making themselves stronger. Increasing Strength Excercise for starters. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar impersonates with lies and disguise. A Lunar impersonates by stealing the guys face and perfectly duplicating his manerisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes no difference wether you fly with a spell or with shapeshifted wings, why does it make a difference if you impersonate with a Charm (let's say Perfect Mirror, which is explicitly so good it can't be detected with normal senses) or a shape-shfted face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T19:08:07-08:00","id":342486,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I would posit that first, aesthetics are probably the most important part of the game. As aesthetics, in this case, would cover ensuring that every player is inhabiting the same game worl<br /> <br /> Second, there's a particular kind of monster-development in Prototype. The apothesis of the Blacklight Virus is an abominable protean horror, it points at a particular progression that makes the individual <i>less human </i>and <i>more monster. </i>The Prototype characters (spoiler not-withstanding) turn from person into thing. IMO they're best expressed as Wyld or unique Sorcerous Project created Behemoths.<br /> <br /> In any case, a Lunar doesn't do this becoming thing. The Lunar express Luna's contradictions by being both more monster and more human. At their apotheosis they are equally heroes and behemoths. When they inspire horror, it is a <i>Holy </i>Horror. The earth doesn't recoil at their power, it thrums at their notice. Shadows grow larger, the beat at the heart of the jungle begins to pound in the ears, the desert sands rise and howl in testament. The greatest shapes of Lunar power are not twisted gestalt creatures, but immortal and primal World Forces older than men and greater than gods.<br /> <br /> These are very different things, they express very different games.<br /> <br /> So, Mercer &amp; company might look kinda visually like a Lunar, but the two are actually very different because of their origins/themes/what their aesthetics mean.<br /> <br /> These are aesthetics, but these aesthetics matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 12-16-2014, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T19:28:59-08:00","id":342503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I fly with wings or fly with a spell, I'm still flying.<br /> <br /> The <b>What</b> is what's important, not the <b>How</b> or<b> Why</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still inaccurate. The How absolutely matters. When the How stops mattering, <i>you get Silver Solars</i>. <br /> <br /> And again, all the Mercer aesthetics are fine,<i> if the Lunar Sacred Hunts something creepy that would have those powers/aesthetics and expresses them through wearing that shape</i>. As native Lunar Charms, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T19:39:33-08:00","id":342525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that once you get past how the powers look, there's more Lunarry things than non lunarry things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is that you're determined that the presentation and theming doesn't matter and a ot of the pushback you are getting from people is trying to say 'No, actually, these things are extremely important'.<br /> <br /> It's just not true that any insance of supernatural attributes, plus eating people, plus shapeshifting will be good Lunar material. Just as it's not true that all Lunars have supernatural attributes (OK, that one's <b>hard</b> but you could do it), or shapeshift, or eat people. Lunars aren't just a bunch of elements thrown in a bucket, they're elements put together in a particular way with deliberate themes. One of the consequences of that is that the temes that Prototype basically runs in fall in the box labeled Chimera, just like the themes from The Thing, and a lot of the ones belonging to the T-1000.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T19:41:24-08:00","id":342527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alex doesn't become a Monster until the sequel, after he lost faith in humanity. If anything, he starts out as a monster and becomes more human.<br /> <br /> James Heller starts human and ends up a human with monstrous powers. You can see it in his actions. His motivation boils down to &quot;Murder the people responsible for the death of my family and fuck everything else&quot; and then, when he finds out his daughter is alive, it changes to &quot;rescue my daughter and fuck everything else&quot;<br /> <br /> Aesthetics is meaningless when you're talking about &quot;I want to make a character that can do stuff kinda like these guys. What can I do?&quot;<br /> &quot;Do you mind having mythical animals and legendary beast themes?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let me clarify, I'm not talking about a moral quality of monstrous, rather I'm speaking only of the physical qualities / the way that such a creature might make a person feel.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how compassionate / upstanding an individual undergoing the Blacklight virus may be, they will come across as monstrous. After a certain point in their progression, they are other than human; <i>things</i> even if in their minds/outlook/values are unchanged from that of their human selves / any given human, the thing they become is other than human. In form, it's an abomination.<br /> <br /> If someone plays in my game and wants to make a character exactly like the protagonist in the Prototype games, I'd probably point them towards an Abyssal (especially in light of the Ex 3E previews). The character themes in Prototype are incompatible to Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:23:20-08:00","id":342560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm specifically talking about the end result. The aesthetics can go to hell, I'm not talking about Aesthetics. I'm talking about what they actually do.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Once more, talking about abillities, not themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've made this very clear. The fact that you've had to keep making it clear should be a good sign that others don't see that the end results are all that matter, and that themes and presentation are important.<br /> <br /> To go back to your original question: Why do people not like this as inspiration? For reasons you're determined not to talk about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","user":"SuddenThunder","date":". 12-16-2014, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:27:10-08:00","id":342563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Lunar's abillity to sacred Hunt things that fit the Mercer Aesthetic, is in itself a native Lunar ability. As is their ability to sacred hunt <i>anything. </i>And to take the form of things they sacred hunted. Or forms derived from things they sacred hunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and this is kind of a confusing concept. Because Sacred Hunting is a &quot;native power&quot; but the form of a Teodozija is not: even when you're wearing it, you're that specific demon. The shapeshifting itself is the native power. The collateral abilities tied to the shape you've taken are not really &quot;native&quot; in a sense so much as &quot;borrowed for the duration of being in that shape.&quot;<br /> <br /> Put another way: if you eat some elemental with a whipfist, sure you'll have whipfist in that shape. But that's because the elemental's shape has the trait: whipfist and you're wearing that shape, not because &quot;whipfirst&quot; is an intrinsically Lunar thing. (I know you specifically disclaimed whipfist but this is the easiest example for me to describe).<br /> <br /> This is quite different from expressing otherwise-very-human excellence (Charms) through the lens of Attributes instead of Abilities. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:10:14-08:00","id":342578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the only difference I can see is the &quot;Biological Horror&quot; look verses the &quot;Mythical God Beast&quot; look, and what it look like is the least important thing</div> </div> </div> </div>First, just because you decalre something 'irrelevant' or 'least important' doesn't make it so. The ongoing conversation here about just that point demonstrates that it's important to a number of your peers. <br /> <br /> Second, the developers also thought that distinction was important, enough so that it's specifically the distinction between Lunars and Chimera. Seriously, the Chimera Knack list is basically a Blacklight Virus toolkit. Assimilation of the Prey is their feeding method, Grotesque Psuedopodia for your Whipfist and Tentacle Nova needs, and Perfect Regeneration and Perpetual Regeneration to simulate their survivability. So it's not that no-one thinks this stuff doesn't have a certain shared space with Lunars. It's just that, in Exalted, the Blacklight boys share a bunkhouse with The Thing, and not the silver heroes of the moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:24:11-08:00","id":342585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342578#post342578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the developers also thought that distinction was important, enough so that it's specifically the distinction between Lunars and Chimera. Seriously, the Chimera Knack list is basically a Blacklight Virus toolkit. Assimilation of the Prey is their feeding method, Grotesque Psuedopodia for your Whipfist and Tentacle Nova needs, and Perfect Regeneration and Perpetual Regeneration to simulate their survivability. So it's not that no-one thinks this stuff doesn't have a certain shared space with Lunars. It's just that, in Exalted, the Blacklight boys share a bunkhouse with The Thing, and not the silver heroes of the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small note here: 2e chimeras were horribly, horribly done (both mechanically and aesthetically) and should not be taken as either remotely good design or anything resembling future design intent.<br /> <br /> That is probably part of the reason that people (including devs IIRC) disclaim Prototype as Lunar inspiration, because Prototype = 2e chimeraesque. And the &quot;nasty flesh pool of hungry pseudopods&quot; is not the vision that the devs see as thematically appropriate when it comes to Lunar chimerism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 12-17-2014, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:24:29-08:00","id":342586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see people looking at how it looks and not what it is, and then deciding that because it looks strange, it's not Lunarry, even though they're doing amost the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> The only difference Between Mercer's Whipfist and a Squid Totem Lunar turning their arm into a tentacle is what the tentacle looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's quite a difference between having proper anatomy like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cephalopod_limb\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> and effectively being a flesh Alchemical with a Gigeresque phallic blade on the end of what was your arm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with Alex's claw and a Lunar's.<br /> <br /> The How and why of how a character can change shape and eat people and critters to get a new shape is irrelevant tot he fact that they can both do that thing.<br /> </div> </div> </div>You err immensely. Prototype doesn't let either character build up a multitude of shapes. It's the last person you consumed, and you don't get the shape back. This is startlingly similar to the way Abyssal disguise worked in first edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When people realize you're a shapeshifter wit inhuman power, they're going to be scared shitless of you. Biological Horror verses Mythical Godbeast is irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>No, there's a chance they'll worship a godbeast. Not so much if you have a xenomorph tail crossed with a blade on a chain where they would expect a proper arm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're a lot more similar than they're different. Really, the only difference I can see is the &quot;Biological Horror&quot; look verses the &quot;Mythical God Beast&quot; look, and what it look like is the least important thing </div> </div> </div>Well, that, and no running compilation of shapes to choose from. And no animal forms with special capabilities with which to take advantage. And the method by which the protagonist is created. And no unique feature to serve as a Tell, further hammering in the mythical references by having Kolchack Rakshasa hands, a large singular eye, or a fox's tail.<br /> <br /> And yes, this is important. If you just want to reskin everything with the same mechanics, you might want to check out Aberrant. It's a wonderful game for that sort of thing, and the system its revised version is set to use is getting publicly playtested soon. But this just isn't the way Exalted was set up; one of the stated design goals was to make things that look dissimilar also feel mechanically dissimilar, to further the &quot;unique kung fu technique&quot; feeling of getting Charms that are not the same between different character types. This is why Silver Solar is bad, and why several of the shtick-stealing Solar Charms from the old version of Dreams of the First Age were so beyond the pale that they were completely thrown out and replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:27:04-08:00","id":342588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342585#post342585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small note here: 2e chimeras were horribly, horribly done (both mechanically and aesthetically) and should not be taken as either remotely good design or anything resembling future design intent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, there's never been a mechanical implementation of anything remotely Lunar that really worked ... I was just making a 'here's your themes' point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:30:12-08:00","id":342589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There, Lunar that takes inspiration from Prototype and uses it's Lunar abilities in the same way as a Blacklight host would use their's.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I don't see a lot of Prototype in that. It could just as well be based on 'Infamous: Second Son' or and generic revenge story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:36:29-08:00","id":342592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=342588#post342588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's never been a mechanical implementation of anything remotely Lunar that really worked ... I was just making a 'here's your themes' point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha fair enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:48:14-08:00","id":342597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their, Alex Mercer's complete Playable Powerset as a Lunar without any of his Biohorror imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>But now what makes it Alex Mercer in particular, rather than a random bunch of powers thrown together?<br /> <br /> Sure you can throw away all that character's theming, but then you've bascally discarded the character. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T21:50:27-08:00","id":342599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I keep telling you people that the looks are irrelevant because they are.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't get to dictate that.<br /> <br /> As for as the Thing being a mindless beast, check this out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T22:09:01-08:00","id":342605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire point is isperation in the form of &quot;I want to do that&quot; is not in anyway related to what the &quot;That&quot; looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>So ... why is this even a discussion? If you don't have any particular desire to do something that's recognisable as Prototype, and everything on your shopping list of powers is already in the Lunar book. what does it matter what the rest of us think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T22:28:18-08:00","id":342634,"title":"","content":"So basically it comes down to, the OP wants his Lunars to take some cues from Prototype, The rest of the forum things this is a terrible idea. <br /> <br /> So just go for it and don't care what the forum says, man. You don't need to have your Exalted inspirations align with what people in this particular forum says. By forum standards about 3/4s of the Exalted campaigns I've played and half of my characters probably wouldn't count as &quot;real&quot; Exalted, and I had plenty of fun :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T22:44:05-08:00","id":342645,"title":"","content":"I'm happy this derail was taken out of the wishlist thread. That's awesome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You started talking aesthetics <b><i>after </i></b>I brought it up</div> </div> </div> </div>And we'd already talked about them <i>before</i> you posted for the third time on the subject; the third post being the one I quoted.<br /> <br /> It didn't seem to me like you needed to ask the question again when we'd already answered it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd also like you to note that &quot;Rip a guys arms off and graft it onto youself&quot; is not the same as &quot;turn into something after you hunt and eat it&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'd like you to note how I pointed out that Flesh aspected Charms include ways to more efficiently take someone's flesh into your own to steal their strength. Why would you think &quot;Alex Mercer's total-body Consume power&quot; would not be possible with those Charms?<br /> <br /> Certainly, you're not going to see a Lunar absorb and kill a whole struggling human being with her skin alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and If I give claws to my Liminal, chances are it's goon have claws 24 seven, which is not shapeshifting, it's surgery. </div> </div> </div>Why are you assuming that Flesh-oriented zombie/frankenstein-Exalts would lack the power to transform their hands into blades or claws? The Breath-aspected powers will allow control over wind, and Soil-aspected powers can create and control zombies. Liminals are going to have some &quot;out there&quot; dramatic powers to play with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you might disagree about Alex's <i>character </i>being poor inspiration, but I was talking about his<i> abillities, </i> </div> </div> </div>So was I. The Liminal Exalted are a much better fit for his abilities, not just his background. For one thing, Liminals don't have Animal Totems. Alex Mercer never turns into an animal, he always shapeshifts into the likeness of another human being. That's easily within the possibility for a Liminal disguise Charm.<br /> <br /> His disguises are also only skindeep, since he still smells exactly like his unnatural, bio-monster self, and retains his full Attributes and powers no matter what his outer surface appears. He's still just as heavy, and probably looks the same in infrared vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-17-2014, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T23:51:41-08:00","id":342689,"title":"","content":"You can totally use Prototype as inspiration for Lunar characters. Probably the more murder-fest types, but that's pretty typical in most video games.<br /> <br /> I can very much see a person bringing a friend over who knows nothing of Exalted and showing her Prototype. &quot;This is the sort of thing a Lunar Exalt can do. Not exactly the same, but pretty darn close in many ways. Much moreso than most any other video game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's not forget that not all Lunars are going to be the same, just like every other kind of Exalt. Protean horror can easily be a fringe of the Lunar experience, just as a fey-minded trickster could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:05:47-08:00","id":342697,"title":"","content":"As a reminder, a Sacred Hunt requires only a bit of blood; a Lunar need not consume the entirety of its kill's biomass, Tyranid-style, to be able to assume its form.<br /> <br /> Guilty as I've been of it in the past, I'm still rapidly tiring of folks &quot;simplifying&quot; the process of the Sacred Hunt to &quot;he eats them lol.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:52:07-08:00","id":342710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I want to know why Protptype is considrered a bad source of inspiration for Lunar Characters when the hard limits of Alex and Jame's powers are, hoethey use those powers, and what those powers actually do, once you strip away the biohorror, are pretty much bread and butter Lunar things, and that James Heller's original is pretty typical Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when people give you their reasons you keep saying 'that's irrelevant' or 'that doesn't matter'. It's clear that you don't think these things matter, but reasons only have to matter to the people who have them and no amount of telling people that their reasons are out of bounds for the conversation is going to be helpful in sorting this out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious as to why &quot;Biohorror&quot; is being conflated with &quot;shapeless Protean mass of flesh&quot; and &quot;Rubberman&quot; when Alex's powers really aren't that diferant from a standard Lunar's once you get past how it looks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is at least in some part because that's the conflation the published Exalted material gives us when it talks about Chimera. When you want to draw from an inspiration that is very obviously already present in the setting, and ask why it isn't something else ... you're going to have an uphill climb. <br /> <br /> But you don't want to talk about themes and presentation, so ...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T02:10:24-08:00","id":342738,"title":"","content":"Prototype can certainly be a fine source of inspiration for a Lunar character. Hunting enemies, taking their forms or just parts of their form and/or their memories are definately things Lunars can do, and which will be in theme. If you have the knacks for hunting demons/elementals/fae you can even go for the aesthetics. Even becoming more monstrous and inhuman is in theme, looking at Raksi, Ma-Ha-Sushi and other elder Lunars.<br /> <br /> When re-imagining any character from another property to Exalted there will of course always be certain concessions in theme and/or aestethics. However, when compared to other sources of inspiration for Lunars quoted in this or other threads (such as spiderman), Heller or Mercer will be much easier to create as a Lunar, at least in methods used and even looks.<br /> <br /> In the theme department you will have to build in some reluctance, or loathing towards his or her Lunar exaltation to reflect that in the original property the source of his power is a creepy body-horror virus and not something which the character considers a blessing. Take a Spirit Shape that the character dislikes for some reason, or better yet, some permanent limit and a chimera knack or two. Perhaps the character has a personal hatred for Luna because the event he survived that earned his exaltation (or the subsequent Wyld Hunt) resulted in the death of his loved ones. Season with some burning desire for revenge and the willingness to shed rivers of blood, and voil\u00e0, a Lunar Prototype expy in Creation.<br /> <br /> I suspect the fact that Mercer and Heller's powers are not a blessing, but a curse, and at best a tool to exact revenge is why people are reluctant to describe Prototype as general Lunar inspiration (as opposed to inspriration for a particular Lunar), but lean more towards Abyssals. This is after all a defining aspect of Prototype's narrative. However with the caveats that in Exalted being a Lunar is a gift from above, and is usually more animal oriented in the shapeshifting department, you can certainly use Prototype as a way to describe Lunars to new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T04:33:56-08:00","id":342787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I want to know why Protptype is considrered a bad source of inspiration for Lunar Characters when the hard limits of Alex and Jame's powers are, hoethey use those powers, and what those powers actually do, once you strip away the biohorror, are pretty much bread and butter Lunar things, and that James Heller's original is pretty typical Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who want Prototype as an inspiration for Lunars want Lunars to specifically be about biohorror stuff. They want Lunars to look more like Alex Mercer, with the big crazy claw arms and the cancerous looking red and black extrusions and the hammer fists and the complete chitinous shell and sucking people up by erupting into a mass of fibers that engulfs them because they dislike therianthrope mythology. Same as why some people want Lunars to be more like a Taoist sorcerer who was born from an uncanny confluence of cosmic energies in the incidental shape of a mundane monkey <i>rather than therianthrope mythology</i>. Or even when people say that they want Lunars to have associations with things that look like some New Age alien things.<br /> <br /> You're going against the grain of what the developers actually mean when they say that Lunars won't really draw much inspiration from Prototype.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:38:34-08:00","id":342882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I'm not one of those people. I'm the guy who is pointing out that when you ignore what it looks like, the way those powers do and are used to do some of the same things as Lunar powers, that the basic plot of the games fits pretty well as a Lunar narrative, and hell, the guy from the second game has a pretty good Lunar origin story.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point of all this? If we wind up having Lunars that maintain the same tone and aesthetic they've always had and you have no problem with that whatsoever, then what are you arguing for? Has somebody impugned on Prototype's honour, and it requires a voice to speak in its defence?<br /> <br /> Even if Prototype fit exactly with Lunars, there would probably be no diminishment whatsoever from it not specifically being a source of inspiration, anymore than they can use the innumerable other things which are just as or even more fitting as specific sources of inspiration, because who has the time to read all of that?<br /> <br /> When you render Prototype down to the basics like this, maybe there's nothing dissonant to it, but there's nothing to really distinguish it either, so who cares?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, I'm being told I'm wrong by people who are fixated on the biohorror look, or the sword arm, or the &quot;Shoggoth-rubberman&quot; comparison, and they keep going back to that no matter how many times I explain why the biohorror aesthetic is irrelevant or how the shoggoth rubberman thing is the exact opposite of accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're saying has nothing to do with why people want Prototype <i>specifically</i> as an inspiration for Lunars, and why the developers are refuting them with the idea that it's not the direction they're going with. <br /> <br /> Nothing about Prototype makes it important enough to add to the pile of Lunar inspirations, and even if your arguments were enough to make it so, we'd still wind up with something that wouldn't really resemble Prototype more than it resembled various other things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 12-17-2014, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:57:14-08:00","id":342892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Becuase my argument is &quot;I know it's differant, but when you strip away the biohorror visuals, these guys are actually a lot like a Lunar</div> </div> </div> </div>We understand your argument. You've been very clear. <br /> <br /> It just seems like, to me and I imagine a number of the other poster's here, very much the same sort of argument as 'well you can strip out the lungs, and the liver, and at least one of those kidneys, but it's still actually a lot like a working human'. It's sort of a 'sum of the parts' argument that very much misses the point of the subject being an entity with it's own theming and presentation rather than a bunch of interchangable game mechanics. <br /> <br /> We understand you don't think these things are important. You don't seem to understand that many of us think they are, and no amount of simply saying 'No, I'm not going to talk about that' will change that position. <br /> <br /> And you did ask for us to share our thoughts and reasons with you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I even explained both a way to make a character arc inspired by prototype sans biohorror and a way to explain most of Mercer's abilities in a Lunar Mythic God-beast Context.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in doing so stripped away anything distinctive that might have identified the source material as being Prototype. There's a long standing thread here about taking inspiration and moving it into exalted and (although we can't do the experiment now because the answer is public) I would bet that if you had posted that descriptive arc, no-one would have picked it as having come from Prototype. You would have had to explain it just as you did here, and if you have to do a detailed explaination to make your inspiration work, then it's hardly very 'inspiring'. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once more, what it looks like and how it's presented is irrelevent compared to what it does and how it's used</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you keep saying that but you've never supported it. It's just a truism that you keep repeating over and over even though it's been disputed many times. Do you actually have any support for it? Is there anywhere in exalted that what it looks like and how it's presented is irrelevant?<br /> <br /> There are two strong counterexamples I would point to. Gods and Elementals strongly indicate that presentation matters in Exalted. They are, in almost all ways, mechanically identical. They draw from the same Charms and they're goverened by the same rules (with some corner cases), but they're not the same thing. And I don't think you'd run into many players mistaking them for the same thing. <br /> <br /> The other example would be Abyssals. Sure there's a bit more differentiation here but it's mostly in pursuit of the aesthetic. A significant number of their Charms are exactly the same and a number of the others are just adjusted for tone. To paraphrase, when you take out the gothic horror, these guys look a lot like Solars. But no-one is mistaking sources of Solar inspiration for Abyssal heroes, and vice-versa. <br /> <br /> Exalted is a game in which the presentation, the aesthetics, the theming, all of these things do actually matter. They've mattered since the very beginning. They're the primary distinction in same cases between things which are pretty important to keep distinct. If you want to convince people otherwise you're going to have to put more effort in than just saying 'no'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:08:19-08:00","id":342897,"title":"","content":"Let me preface this by warning you that I haven't played Prototype. Based on my limited understanding of it, I would say it's OK as an inspiration for Lunars. Not good, and not terrible - just OK.<br /> <br /> My reasoning for this is that, as you say, once you get over the visual effects of the Blacklight characters' powers, the basic mechanics of how they work are a reasonably good match to Lunar shapeshifting shticks. <i>However, </i>this is a very narrow lens to look at Lunars through. Lunars are supposed to have a lot of things going for them besides shapeshifting - a unique social context (Anathema to some, folk heroes to others), a divine connection (Luna personally visits every Lunar at least once, allegedly), a range of charms that have little or nothing to do with Shapeshifting, plus the usual set of baggage that comes just from being a character in Creation.<br /> <br /> It's about as valid an inspiration as Sun Wukong (<u><i>Journey to the West</i></u> - who was never human and is crazy-OP), Bigby Wolf (<i><u>Fables</u></i> - also not really a human), or Elfman Strauss (<u><i>Fairy Tail</i></u> - another Lunar-y guy with none of the Lunar baggage.)<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't recommend Prototype to most people as a Lunar example, specifically because they're going to think of the flesh-tentacles first and the mechanics second, and not get any of the other themes. If nothing else, this thread has proved that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:18:10-08:00","id":343024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two strong counterexamples I would point to. Gods and Elementals strongly indicate that presentation matters in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in <i>Megamind</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T11:34:44-08:00","id":343123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=343024#post343024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in <i>Megamind</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Welcome to the jungle!~&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T13:41:33-08:00","id":343162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe I've provided a re-skinned Alex, thus proving that appearance means nothing to powers, and there's very little difference between one kind of &quot;Human mind in the body of a pants soilingly terrifying protean monster&quot; and an other, and chhances are you're going to just as terrified of the one that turns into a TRex, a 12 foot bear man, and a squid as you are the one that turns into a mass of teeth and tentacles, a 6 foot armored bodybuilder, and a clawed horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you made a Lunar who is inspired by Alex Mercer? Great! Good on you. That does not mean that Prototype as a whole should apply to Lunars as a whole. Lunars are very much Mythical Shapeshifters, not the Protean, Amorphous shapeshifter powers of Prototype.<br /> <br /> Let me make one thing very clear to you though, the appearance of a power DOES matter, in fact, I'd go so far as say that it's the most important thing about a power, at least in this medium.<br /> If there's an Infernal Presence charm that works because the Infernal <span style=\"color:#008000\">SPEAKS WITH THE PRESENCE OF MALFEAS, THE DEMON CITY</span>, and thus is capable of convincing the <span style=\"color:#008000\">WEAK, PATHETIC MORTALS</span> to <span style=\"color:#008000\">KNEEL</span> to him, and there's a Solar charm that convinces people to accept a Solar as their king, because he has the aura of a born leader, they will probably have similar mechanics, yet feel completely different to the player.<br /> <br /> It's all about presentation when it comes to powers, because, at the end of the day, what we're really doing here is adjusting some numbers on a sheet of paper and rerolling some die. That's what a Charm really is, and it's the way that it's presented that that makes it interesting. It's one of the reasons why I love that every Charm has an over-the-top kung fu name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:05:25-08:00","id":343218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;Lunars can't do prototype&quot; tell me that if I want to make a Lunar who chooses Shape shifting as his primary tool, and wants to hunt down and devour mighty beasts in order to graft their physical attributes atop his own in order to become strong enough to accomplish his goals, that I'm doing it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> No it doesn't. The context of the developer statement that establishes why it doesn't has been laid out in exacting detail for you. When they say &quot;we're not basing Lunars on Alex Mercer&quot;, they are not referring to <i>anything you are talking about</i>. This entire thread is based on the most exceeding degree of obtuseness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T14:51:37-08:00","id":343307,"title":"","content":"If imagery and presentation aren't an issue couldn't you just take the &quot;mythic beast&quot; inspired powers and reskin them as blacklight virus charms I mean kraken tentacle explosion or whatever they call it can easily be whipfist just reverse what people here are saying if it fits a character better I don't think anyone here will accuse you of badwrongfun or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/659-dominostro","name":"Dominostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T15:20:49-08:00","id":343332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I want to know why the blanket statement was issued instead of a &quot;This part is a nono but this part is applicable...No not that part, this part that's kinda already like what we're doing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they don't want to be locked into specific expectations if they later change their minds on certain things. And they don't want to leak acceptable/unacceptable themes until they're ready to, if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T15:48:30-08:00","id":343362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I want to know why the blanket statement was issued instead of a &quot;This part is a nono but this part is applicable...No not that part, this part that's kinda already like what we're doing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I gather that's an ambiguity thing. Rather than list all the ways that the Prototype franchise characters are similar / not similar to Lunars, it's easier to simply say &quot;Lunars aren't this thing&quot; than say Lunars are like these characters, except in x, y, z, etc ways. Lunar vs Mercer/Heller aren't an exhaustive antithesis, but they are different in more ways than they are similar.<br /> <br /> I've seen it suggested in multiple places, but haven't seen you directly reference it (which could just be my laziness, there have been a lot of responses in this thread) how do you feel about Abyssal / Infernal / Other Exalt types work off of the Prototype theme? I would imagine that's the best place to look if you want to play a Blacklight sort of character. <br /> <br /> If you definitely rather play a Lunar and definitely want to play a character like Mercer/Heller, what aspects of their powers do you enjoy the most? What parts of playing a Lunar do you enjoy the most? It appears to me that we are not going to be able to reconcile our points of view (a good thing, variety/spice of life/etc cliche) so in light of that let's try approaching the question in another way.<br /> <br /> You seem to be focusing a lot on the fact that Lunars <br /> <br /> A) kill and eat others to take their form<br /> B) are survivors<br /> <br /> I feel you could definitely get this from Abyssals, especially in light of Face-Drinking Bite and further support for Renegade Abyssals. I imagine as Abyssal 3E is developed and unveiled we'll be seeing a lot of powers that branch off of this disguise power, which should make Abyssals an even better outlet for Mercer/Heller types.<br /> <br /> How do you feel about playing an Abyssal rather than a Lunar? What would you be missing from the <i>Lunar Narrative</i> in moving from Moon-Power exalt to Death-Power exalt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:14:38-08:00","id":343432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I want to know why the blanket statement was issued instead of a &quot;This part is a nono but this part is applicable...No not that part, this part that's kinda already like what we're doing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Because <i>who cares</i>?! Maybe Vance will have some tolerence for this kind of finickity legalistic form of discourse... in the course of his actual profession, but I know I have no tolerence for it, least of all in defence of fucking Prototype. Unless this is still focused on the &quot;if they say it won't be like Prototype, that extends to every slightest detail of Prototype&quot; argument, in which case the basic retort is that nobody would think like that. We might as well have a thread complaining about how Lunars obviously won't be men, or act in cities, or have voices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:49:27-08:00","id":343452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because &quot;Lunars can't do prototype&quot; tell me that if I want to make a Lunar who chooses Shape shifting as his primary tool, and wants to hunt down and devour mighty beasts in order to graft their physical attributes atop his own in order to become strong enough to accomplish his goals, that I'm doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> That using my heartsblood pool to steal someones face and my intelligence charms to absorb their memories and manipulation charms to perfectly duplicate their mannerisms and then use all of that to infiltrate a place is not a thing Lunar spies should be doing.<br /> <br /> That if I want to play a character who stays in his human form and grows fangs, claws, and other assorted natural weaponry in combat will not receive support and thus will be inferior to the guy who has a giant silver hammer and the 12 foot tall anthropomorphic grizzly bear.<br /> <br /> It tells me that Lunars, who based on method of Exaltation should be the hard core determinator survivor types should not be hard core determinators.<br /> <br /> It tells me that revenge plots are inappropriate goals for a Lunar<br /> <br /> But that's wrong. All of that is or should be something a Lunar who specialized in shifting should be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all of these are things that Lunars are able to do. All of that is already in the book, and none of it is really in dispute by anyone. <br /> <br /> Prototype isn't being cast into some sort of void where nothing that was done in Prototype can ever be done by Lunars at all, even when that stuff is very generic and done in ample other media that is a direct inspiration for Lunars. It's just that none of the distinctive elements of Prototype, the things that make it Prototype in particular including it's themes and presentation are considered to be fertile material for Lunar inspiration.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T16:56:16-08:00","id":343457,"title":"","content":"When people were talking about Prototype as Lunar inspiration beforehand, they were talking about the parts you're specifically excluding. That is why the things they said, at the time, do not apply to the stuff you're interested in.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what else there is to say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T17:44:11-08:00","id":343486,"title":"","content":"Well, we should just make Cole McGrath be an Exigent of the god of Lightning and then let him and the OP's Prototype Lunar duke it out to see who wins.<br /> Yes, this is me injecting some silliness to this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T18:54:08-08:00","id":343535,"title":"","content":"To say that you can strip out all the bio-horror pseudopoda biomass-devouring stuff from Prototype and have it be a good Lunar inspiration is a lot like arguing Hitler is a good Lunar inspiration once you divorce him from all the Nazi bits.<br /> <br /> Technically true, but pointless. And likely to mislead people when you publish it. Do we want to go over DBs and element-bending again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T18:58:15-08:00","id":343538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They work better for the aesthetic, but are terrible models for the Mechanic-the how the powers work and what they're used for, and the actual &quot;This is how it works, this is how you do it, and this is what it's good for&quot; is whats important<br /> <br /> The themes of &quot;hunting down a monster, defeating it in battle, killing it, and after doing so eating it in order to take it's power for my own&quot; and the &quot;Shapeshifting&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what drew me to Prototype, and that's what drew me to the Lunars<br /> <br /> The other similarities I pointed out were things I noticed later-the similar nature of how the powers worked, similar limitations(gotta be something ya ate), and the similar ways the powers can be used were things I noticed later. The &quot;wait a minute, most of their non-shifting powers are basically just super attributes and augmented sense&quot; thing, which are a core Lunar thing and a thing they can easily do are things I noticed later and thought &quot;hey maybe I can play a Lunar that's kinda like that&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Mechanics of the shapeshifting and the ability to take more than one extra form, and the ability to combine aspects of various forms to augment my already superhuman attributes, and the focus on super human skills(Ability Charms) rather than Super Human Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm pretty sure this is something we can work with...<br /> <br /> As far as mechanics go, you're asking this in terms of 3e (citing Lunars as now being cast as Mythic God-Monsters rather than . . .whatever Lunar were supposed to be in 1e &amp; 2e) so my first and most primary suggestion is to wait to see what the Dev's come up with for Infernals / Liminals / Abyssals. I imagine a particularly strange Exigent could work for this as well. Since no one is yet saying which splat is coming out when, aside from Dragonbloodeds next and then Exigents, the latter are probably your best bet.<br /> <br /> The Finding-Killing-Becoming thing is still a thing for Lunars. What appears to be less absolute is the ability for Lunars to combine those shapes in bizzare gesthalt creations. <br /> <br /> My suggestion is to wait to see what the Dev's come up with, it's possible that the mechanics you're looking for will be more available down the line in the future. At the very least, I imagine Exigents could play off Attributes just as easily as Lunar's could.<br /> <br /> - - - - <br /> <br /> As for the blow back this thread seems to be generating, I feel like it's largely because you're looking at the characters as collections of powers. All the things you're describing are things Lunars do, rather than things Lunars are.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, whether or not Prototype fits with your idea of a Lunars Mechanics is up to you and your storyteller. But the themes of a Lunar, their history and character and what their powers say about who they are isn't ever going to jive with Mercer/Heller, they're very different kinds of characters/stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T18:58:27-08:00","id":343539,"title":"","content":"What the christ this is the first time I've seen a Lunars thread go full Godwin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:07:28-08:00","id":343546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=343539#post343539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the christ this is the first time I've seen a Lunars thread go full Godwin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were you present on the old forums?<br /> <br /> I forget.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:08:37-08:00","id":343549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=343546#post343546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were you present on the old forums?<br /> <br /> I forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which iteration. I was definitely on the forum since at least 2007, maybe even a year or so earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:09:37-08:00","id":343550,"title":"","content":"The devs did not make a blanket statement against bio-horror when they said &quot;Lunars aren't Alex Mercer.&quot; They explicitly rejected scifi influences in other quotes. All of which are available if you go look or at least ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T19:24:57-08:00","id":343563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=343538#post343538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What appears to be less absolute is the ability for Lunars to combine those shapes in bizzare gesthalt creations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man I hope not! Errata'd HBR was too much fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T20:00:37-08:00","id":343595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not an ability of defualt Lunars, which will be a devastating loss, it certainly should be an abillity possesed by 3E Chimerae, who going by developer coments are basically just Normal Lunars who grafted some Extra Bits onto their Totemistic Spirit Shape<br /> <br /> Nah. Heller is very much a Lunaresque character. He got his powers after surviving a whole lot of horrible shit and I could very much see a Lunar going through his story. He just needs a Totem and a change of imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, then we have an ontological disagreement. In which case I tip my hat and bid you good day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:37:45-08:00","id":346069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's been brought up a few times is the Idea that Liminals might be better for making a &quot;Prototype&quot; inspired Character.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to this we've been told about is that the default Liminal Origin is vaugly like Alex Mercer's Origin(except not really, the evidence for &quot;new person in old body&quot; is no more conclusive than the evidence of &quot;has amnesia because dying tends to take oxygen away frm the brain&quot;) and a statement on What we know about Liminals maybe being able to improve their bodies by taking limbs and organs from others and grafting them onto their own body in replacement of their own sub par body members.<br /> <br /> How does &quot;Self Modifying Frankenstein's Monster&quot; translate into &quot;Shape-shifting Monster with the mind of a super intelligent human, who takes new forms by hunting down and devouring others, and can combine aspects of it's various forms to bestow natural weaponry upon it'self?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean-type stuff is only one of the inspirations that went into Liminal Soup. The list given some time ago was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A few: Promethean: the Created. Kindred of the East. The old &quot;Risen&quot; supplement for Wraith. Mary Shelley's Frankenstein, or: The Modern Prometheus. The mangas &quot;Claymore&quot; and &quot;Berserk.&quot; The Ultimate Spider-Man &quot;Clone Saga&quot; storyline.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:48:28-08:00","id":346076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How does &quot;Self Modifying Frankenstein's Monster&quot; translate into &quot;Shape-shifting Monster with the mind of a super intelligent human, who takes new forms by hunting down and devouring others, and can combine aspects of it's various forms to bestow natural weaponry upon it'self?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Liminals actually have Body-horror as an aesthetic, and considering one of their themes is that they're monsters that fight worse monsters (like the Prototype protagonists), there are actually a few similarities.<br /> <br /> The problem is, of course, that we don't know a whole lot about the abilities that the Liminals have, except that they can replace parts of themselves and are REALLY hard to kill, neither of which are abilities they get from their Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:17:59-08:00","id":346319,"title":"","content":"Liminals are explicitly promised to get a Bone-aspected Charm to grow bone armor over their bodies. Flesh Aspect is called out as the source of violence and physical attack power.<br /> <br /> Why WOULDN'T the Flesh Charms have Mercer's Devastator attacks? Plus Whipfist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:55:09-08:00","id":346361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=346319#post346319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liminals are explicitly promised to get a Bone-aspected Charm to grow bone armor over their bodies. Flesh Aspect is called out as the source of violence and physical attack power.<br /> <br /> Why WOULDN'T the Flesh Charms have Mercer's Devastator attacks? Plus Whipfist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly if those powers are in any way influenced, even in the tiniest bit, by Flesh Shintai from KotE. The Discipline that started with grotesquely stretching limbs or a neck and progressed on through some admittedly weird side-tracks (euphoric breath weapon WTF?) to arrive at full-body shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T20:52:21-08:00","id":346404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that doesn't feel very in theme with what we've been told about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Hunting down and eating something to get it's shape and power&quot; is not the same as &quot;grafting this guy's limbs to my body&quot; </div> </div> </div>A Liminal spots a guy who has something she wants, she hunts him down and kills him, and she uses the proposed Flesh Charm to absorb his entire body into hers -- much more efficient than having to perform surgery, and it means she doesn't have to give up any of her current body parts. No muss, no fuss, no downside.<br /> <br /> You never explain why you feel Mercer's Consume ability wouldn't be an appropriate mastery for Liminals to achieve through their Flesh-manipulating powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and any natural weapons or what have you that are grafted on are likely to be permanent rather than something you can manifest or demanifest at will. </div> </div> </div>Based on what insider knowledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:33:54-08:00","id":346477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because at no point on what we know are we told any abilities of a Liminals will involve shape-shifting or absorbing biomas directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the EX3 backer preview? On the last page, it notes that their Charms allow them to perform &quot;even more impressive feats of body-theft&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're told, essentially, that their hard mofos to put down, and that they have a vaguely defined power to take the limbs or organs of others and graft them to their body time improve themselves. </div> </div> </div>Vaguely defined, in the context of the Charm concept above, can cover an awful lot of ground toward Liminals being as close as you can get to Prototype in Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Grafting a Tiger Arm to your torso is not the same as killing a tiger to gain it's power, and then using the tiger's power to grow a clawed arm. </div> </div> </div>And at what point in Prototype do you have an opportunity to do either? The entirety of the power suite seems geared toward collecting points from killing and then progressing along a set of powers that has nothing to do with the lives consumed, save for their use as raw fuel. Lunars need to synthesize, not simply subsume.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I'fd ask you what insider knowledge you have. And again, Lik to that bone Carapace charm these Marrow Aspects are supposed to be getting, because that's not on what we know either. </div> </div> </div>There are some questions I do recall Sunder, or someone, asking, exactly because Lunar inspiration has been incredibly contentious in the past, particularly with regard to characters in popular media. These discussions are why I twitch when someone mentions Mystique... or Mercer. And to get back to the idea of this paragraph, the long and short of it is that the Abyssal makeover is going to result in a reduction of the &quot;icky undead&quot; stuff, which fits neatly at home with the fact that Liminals are often icky and always undead, being wonderful foils for Abyssals as life-from-death as opposed to life touched by death.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the possibility of KotE influence here. The most relevant Shintai Disciplines likely being Blood, Bone and Flesh. Jade seems a bit out of place, and Ghost-Flame even more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T08:20:01-08:00","id":346671,"title":"","content":"I doubt that the limb-attachment is going to be too permanent, particularly if Claymore is playing into it. Characters tend to aim for cutting off limbs and then dicing them up because they know that limb reattachment is easy... if it isn't interrupted by dicing up the severed member with a rapid speed sword attack.<br /> <br /> Prototype 2 sounds slightly more structured for Lunars in potential, but it's important to note that &quot;survive something that should have killed you&quot; isn't solely the Lunar bag. Armattan survived being stabbed by raiders and had to wander the desert; he became a Zenith. What's more, some Lunars, according to 1e, ended up with their Exaltation because they or their actions were pleasing to Luna.<br /> <br /> RE: Roach as a totem, that's not actually possible unless it's a relatively large roach, which the species we're familiar with loitering around trash and invading homes typically aren't. The vaunted survival capacities of the roach are also based more on their numbers; most people don't usually speak of an individual roach as being unstoppably hardy. They're talking about how there are usually more hiding in unseen locations. In any case, there's another obstacle to totemic beasts for Heller, and that's the absolute rejection of a totem concept by the narrative and the underlying assumptions of its genre. Looking at the Let's Play called to mind Aberrant more than it did Exalted. It's quite firmly in the realm of sci-fi superheroics, or superantiheroics, alongside its rival game, Infamous. It's actually super-easy to break tanks in Aberrant, too; if you get even one dot in Mega-Strength, you no longer have to worry about the armor-add on a tank, which means that it only has six points of soak. A punch from someone with Strength 5 (trivial to achieve, since one nova point can get you three Attribute dots) does 7 dice, a kick 9. Add on the Claws power, and you can easily get a few extra dice of damage.<br /> <br /> Contrast with Exalted, where punching a tank up can be much, much more time-consuming, even if it suffers from the maladies of being an inanimate object in terms of how it takes damage. Perhaps it might not strike you as a genre barometer, but it was something that struck me as &quot;hey, this guy totally fits in a game where the lowest level of enhanced strength pretty much pulps people in one hit&quot;. In which case Exalted isn't going to be super-accomodating to the concept no matter what splat you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T09:04:53-08:00","id":346720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=346477#post346477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the last page, it notes that their Charms allow them to perform &quot;even more impressive feats of body-theft&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tell him that over and over again, but he doesn't want to listen.<br /> <br /> If he's closing his ears because he doesn't have the preview and doesn't think I'm actually quoting a source, then he could have the maturity to ask me to verify my source and thus learn about the preview. I'd even quote the damn thing for him.<br /> <br /> Such as these passages:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Liminal Exalted lack the purpose-based Castes of the Celestial Exalted. Instead they are divided into Aspects, somewhat like the Dragon-Blooded. But where Dragon-Blooded are marked by the primacy of elemental Essence running through their veins, Liminal Aspects emphasize elements of life and death. A Liminal\u2019s Aspect is defined by the drives of his creator\u2014different brands of vibrant emotion or obsession produce markedly different Exalts.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects of Flesh</b> are born of creators driven by \u201csavage\u201d passion\u2014vengeance, rage, madness. Flesh represents lust, hunger and thirst, madness and rage. Flesh is the core of identity and the vector of metamorphosis. It is the currency of those caught between life and death. Flesh Aspects are choleric, active, and often aggressive.<br /> <br /> <b>The Power of the Chernozem</b><br /> The Charms of the Liminals derive from the associations of their Aspects and the might of their unnatural bodies. Blood Aspect magic, for example, may allow a Liminal to easily track a man for hundreds of miles with only a sample of bodily fluids to work from, but it also allows confident navigation of the dark waterways and torrential courses of the Underworld, as well as influence over the desires and addictions of others. Soil Charms might bind the dead back into their graves, while just as readily helping the Chernozem bring forth new creations into the world.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the body of a Liminal is incredibly resilient; severed or destroyed limbs may be easily replaced with new ones, and the Liminal\u2019s body soon adapts the new addition so that it looks like a natural part of her form. Moreover, the Chernozem may draw skills and memories from stolen body parts: a Liminal might gain grace from a dancer\u2019s legs, skill from a swordsman\u2019s arm, or guile from a sly man\u2019s tongue. With appropriate Charms, even more impressive and macabre feats of body-theft may be possible. </div> </div> </div>Flesh Charms include themes of lust, hunger, thirst and metamorphosis, and so it is the most likely place for the Liminal Charms that allow &quot;even more impressive and macabre feats of body-theft&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Chernozem are clearly not intended to find organ-transplants and limb-grafting to be the limit of their body-thieving potential. That's just the ground floor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T09:37:45-08:00","id":346743,"title":"","content":"I don't really know or care about Heller. Everything I've heard about his character arc and the story of the game have been bad, so I've refrained from learning even as much about him as I did Alex. (I've never played either game, though I've seen plenty of gameplay.)<br /> <br /> Maybe Heller <i>is </i>closer to proper Lunar inspiration than Mercer. But that doesn't matter as much as Rater thinks.<br /> <br /> Absolutely accurate conversions from one medium or another into Exalted is not the goal. Superman is a prime Solar inspiration, but you're never going to see Solar Charms that shoot heat-rays from your eyes or let you breath hurricanes or maintain constant, effortless levels of superhuman strength, speed and durability.<br /> <br /> There's also the facts that Superman is supposed to be an alien, and his mote-pool is refilled by exposure to sunlight with no actual upper limit to the number of motes he can hold, and he's got an allergy to green space rocks.<br /> <br /> Basically, there are limits to which Superman is a valid influence over Solar Charms. Superman's powers are innate biological features; Solar Charms are learned and practiced skills. That's huge on a foundational level, even if there are superficial, surface-level similarities.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there are some superficial similarities between what Heller can do and what a Lunar could do, but the fundamental justification and genre for them is completely different. Heller is sci-fi, infected by a transformative virus that gives him the ability to improve his flesh and provoke it into cancerous growth and rapid calcification. He absorbs concepts like &quot;mass&quot; and &quot;DNA&quot;. His body ultimately conserves mass, even though it cheats by keeping most of it Elsewhere so that he's merely as heavy as a car instead of a main battle tank (or ten).<br /> <br /> Lunars have never cared about mass. They make new flesh directly from their Essence without needing to eat the whole of what they kill, or to maintain a pocket dimension of spare mass. They can assume forms smaller than human, reducing their weight to whatever is natural to those smaller forms... and this has somehow never made them any less tough than they were at human size.<br /> <br /> Lunars have never cared about DNA. It has always been a successful Hunt which lets them steal the spiritual Essence of their prey, and from there it is their shapeshifting power which lets them express that spirit in a physical form. Blood may mark the end of a successful hunt, but the Hunt is a vast, multifaceted thing, and so blood is not always the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you make a Lunar based on Heller's story and inclinations? Yes. But you cannot make the Lunar Exalted based on Heller's powers. There's enough overlap for tangential inspiration, but it's ultimately a distraction and one is better served looking elsewhere, at the things that get you inspiration not only for those tangential elements, but also far, far more..<br /> <br /> Can you make a Liminal based on Heller's story? Doesn't sound like it. But you CAN (probably) make the Liminal Exalted based on Heller's powers, which belong to the same root source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-21-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:50:55-08:00","id":346864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, these are just those Aesthetic differences that don't matter anywhere near as much as you people seem to think they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they do matter. Because Exalted is an exception-based system rather than an effects-based system. You don't build powers up according to what they do, you start with aesthetics to determine how to differentiate them from other powers and make them look unique. Just as having Charms that do things in a manner that looks Solar is not good for Lunars, so, too, is having Charms that do things in a way that isn't focused on being animalistic shapeshifters, and Prototype tap-dances out of that territory with wild abandon, so it's not really eligible for inspiration-mining except in very peripheral ways that most of the anti-totem fanatics that formerly inhabited the board would have complained bitterly about before opining about their desire to fly &quot;like an emo Peter Pan&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, you can make a Lunar very loosely based on Mercer or Heller, but you're going to have to change so very much of the character that people might need to squint and look very, very hard, since instead of a whipfist he grows a tail with a thagomizer, and proceeds to introduce his enemies to the late Thag Simmons. And he lacks a number of other defining traits, like the devastator, in favor of being able to turn into a sauropod and stomp very heavily on the ground. Also, he doesn't make the ground collapse under him spectacularly from the freakish &quot;extra body mass&quot; he's carrying around (because he isn't in this case, it increases or decreases based on what form he's in), or simply just absorb people like he's absorbing pudding right through his skin, even when wearing clothes.<br /> <br /> And there would be way more flying around as a bird, pouncing from height as a big cat, fighting tanks as a tyrannosaur. Or perhaps he prefers a half-human, half-totem form for kicking ass. And instead of plot-convenient NPCs doing most of the work, he goes into dream trances and sees a confusing series of images that hints at the next mission's objectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T12:24:39-08:00","id":346882,"title":"","content":"Look, Rater, what do you even want?<br /> <br /> Do you want to prove that Lunars are better at being Alex Mercer or Heller than Liminals could be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T12:38:49-08:00","id":346888,"title":"","content":"Any character can be mined for inspiration for a specific kind of Exalt, most can be mined as inspiration for multiple types of Exalted, and if Alex Mercer/James Heller are good inspirations for a Lunar for you, than that's great, more power to you, I hope you enjoy that character. However, I don't think that Prototype as a whole is a good inspiration for Lunars as a whole. You see their similarities, and while I see them too, I get distracted by the differences between them, to the point that I don't consider them a good inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:06:51-08:00","id":346903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You see, these are just those Aesthetic differences that don't matter anywhere near as much as you people seem to think they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have said this a number of times but have made very little effort to prove it and the efforts you have made are unconvincing. It'd be nice if you were at least able to just say &quot;well that's my opinion on the subject&quot; but you don't; you just want to hammer it as some kind of objective fact, which it certainly is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:05:54-08:00","id":346980,"title":"","content":"That is, in my opinion, if anything,even less clear. But, on the other hand, you missed the relevant point. <br /> <br /> See, I, at least, understand why you think aesthetics don't matter. I also think it's a frankly ridiculous position to take which I completely disagree with. I'm not alone. I suspect others who have offered you the opportunity to explain understand just as clearly. They are willing to presume you might have some convincing case to make, as opposed to simply insisting that simply because YOU feel aesthetics don't matter, it means they don't. <br /> <br /> You have been told this before, but I'll try once more: that aesthetics don't matter is your opinion, and you're entitled to it. Others disagree, and insisting repeatedly they are wrong dies not mean they will agree or must agree. I understand your rationale, and I don't. <br /> <br /> Until you get on the same page with others and accept that, to at least SOME folks, aesthetics DO matter, this is going to continue to be an inane discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:42:50-08:00","id":347037,"title":"","content":"Much. Now, consider the situation where one source of inspiration behaves the same way as a splat, but looks different; while a second source of inspiration looks AND behaves like a splat. In that case, the first source is an inferior source of inspiration. Which is just one of several reasons that aesthetics matter to some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T16:50:14-08:00","id":347063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to make a character that is based on a character from an other work, then it is important that the character I make must have powers that a similar enough to the powers of the inspiration, and can be used in the same ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I describe a character as &quot;basically Superman&quot;, I am not saying that he has x-ray vision and heat rays and flight and gets these powers from exposure to his world's sun but loses them when exposed to pieces of his homeland. I'm talking about the <i>aesthetic</i> of superman, which only loosely touches on the things he can do and the reason he can do them. In fact, I would find it quite unexpected if a character described to me as being &quot;like superman&quot; was only like Superman in a mechanical/technical sense, with all the aesthetics being different, because the aesthetics are so core to what Superman is. This is pretty normal. If you don't look at it that way, that's fine, but it looks kind of bad when you go so far out of your way to object to other people doing so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T18:14:07-08:00","id":347088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=347063#post347063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I describe a character as &quot;basically Superman&quot;, I am not saying that he has x-ray vision and heat rays and flight and gets these powers from exposure to his world's sun but loses them when exposed to pieces of his homeland. I'm talking about the <i>aesthetic</i> of superman, which only loosely touches on the things he can do and the reason he can do them. In fact, I would find it quite unexpected if a character described to me as being &quot;like superman&quot; was only like Superman in a mechanical/technical sense, with all the aesthetics being different, because the aesthetics are so core to what Superman is. This is pretty normal. If you don't look at it that way, that's fine, but it looks kind of bad when you go so far out of your way to object to other people doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, completely agree with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T18:48:32-08:00","id":347091,"title":"","content":"I think another fact that is occluding the issue is this: With most every other RPG, there are mechanics (crunch) and description (fluff) and the two tend to be separate. However, in Exalted, the crunch and fluff are so intimately tied together that it is virtually impossible to remove those aesthetics from the power that you wish to use. This is keeping some from seeing beyond the look of the power and just going to what the power does. Exalted writes the Charms for that specific purpose with the fluff before the crunch. There is nothing wrong with that since it enforces the setting. However, it also means that if you want to do X Splat and focus in on only the mechanics of it, then you will not be able to do it without the fluff of X Splat. Superman can be a Solar if you take it as someone who was exiled by their dying parents and now lives in a foreign land and is a paragon of virtue and heroism to those people. But you cannot have him have the Heat Vision and the Flight and such without some major homebrew Charms.<br /> Which, I might add, is the solution here. Do Alex Mercer. Do some homebrew things and use him in a Modern Exalted Shard and have fun with it. But to do it in the regular Exalted universe? It would take some serious compromise in regards to the fluff or the crunch. Either way, you have to give up either what makes a Lunar a Lunar or what makes Mercer, Mercer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T19:39:46-08:00","id":347110,"title":"","content":"When I say my seafaring game's Dawn caste is &quot;like Heracles,&quot; it's not because he's got a Charmset that'd give him a Strength of &quot;however high it needs to be to [do outlandish task].&quot; <br /> <br /> Rather, it's because he's a brash, temperamental warrior, skilled in wrestling, no stranger to sailing, the son of a sky-god, feared for his strength, wielder of a club; because in the past he grappled a magical lion, and is presently on a quest to kill a venomous dragon monster at the behest of his cousin (who leads his people by dint of having been born just a little before he himself was).<br /> <br /> If it was <i>just</i> a matter of being really strong and tough, I could say that <i>Suburban Commando</i>'s Shep Ramsey is an inspiration to the character, which is of course laughable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-22-2014, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T20:35:36-08:00","id":347137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and when I say I want to base a character on James Heller, it's not because I want to play something with a bio-horror aesthetic, it's because I want to play a character who after the loss of his family swore to hunt down and kill the bastards responsible, gained the powers to shape-shift, enhance his physical attributes and fucking eat people and monsters to gain their power and knowledge by surviving a shit tone of stuff being thrown at him by one of the people responsible for the death of his family, and uses the aforementioned &quot;eat things to take their power&quot; ability to gain the knowledge and power to kill that motherfucker and everyone else who gets in his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your family is killed and you swear revenge, and in the process gain the power to take the forms of your enemies to wreak your revenge? Sounds pretty Lunar-y. <br /> <br /> So I don't even understand what your complaint is at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T02:44:09-08:00","id":347293,"title":"","content":"How many times does it have to be said that when developers say &quot;Alex Mercer won't be Lunar inspiration&quot;, they're not talking about every comparable beat in stories or character backgrounds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T03:09:50-08:00","id":347304,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a hybrid body dynamics charm or something exactly for this? You could kill and eat a giant crab, a flea and a wasp, and then give yourself enormous crab arms and creepy giant super legs and gossamer wings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T03:11:38-08:00","id":347305,"title":"","content":"Found it<br /> <br /> A dedicated Lunar can learn to change just part of his body <br /> to gain some special benefit or attack. The character may <br /> transform part of her body, producing any mutation she desires, <br /> so long as the mutation is based on her spirit shape or a shape <br /> in her heart\u2019s blood library. Producing a pox or deficiency costs <br /> 1m, an affliction or debility costs 2m, a blight or deformity <br /> costs 3m, and an abomination costs 4m. These motes are not <br /> committed, the Lunar may simultaneously wear as many muta-<br /> tions as she wishes, and the mutations last as long as the Lunar <br /> desires. Such mutations do not recede when the character\u2019s <br /> anima flares to the 8m+ level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T04:55:10-08:00","id":347322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=347293#post347293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many times does it have to be said that when developers say &quot;Alex Mercer won't be Lunar inspiration&quot;, they're not talking about every comparable beat in stories or character backgrounds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once more, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-22-2014, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T05:43:50-08:00","id":347335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to play a character who after the loss of his family swore to hunt down and kill the bastards responsible, gained the powers to shape-shift, enhance his physical attributes and fucking eat people and monsters to gain their power and knowledge by surviving a shit tone of stuff being thrown at him by one of the people responsible for the death of his family, and uses the aforementioned &amp;quot;eat things to take their power&amp;quot; ability to gain the knowledge and power to kill that motherfucker and everyone else who gets in his way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So ... do that? <br /> <br /> Because you can. You've been able to for two editions now and I would garuntee that there will be absolutely nothing stopping you in X3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T06:15:15-08:00","id":347345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once more, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div> Aaaargh, don't bring algebra into this!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T12:23:37-08:00","id":347604,"title":"","content":"For fucks sake. <br /> <br /> Aesthetics don't matter to you, and this Heller's antics and backstory are such that they can inspire a Lunar. Great, wonderful. But not ALL Lunars will behave like Heller. So he's not a good inspiration for Lunars as a whole. By your own admission Mercer is not a particularly good fit either. <br /> <br /> I could make a Lunar based on Dracula. Yeah-- he survived an army's attempt to destroy his homeland, he has the totem spirit of a wolf, he's strong, he's fast, he has a lost love that's fascinating to him. <br /> <br /> That's valid inspiration for a character , but I think no one, not even you, would argue that vampires are good inspiration for Lunars generally. <br /> <br /> As far as Heller is concerned, you've picked those elements you see as most central to the character, and you've found Lunar inspiration in that.<br /> <br /> Other people may see other elements of Heller as more important than the elements you see as most important. Aesthetic may be one of those other elements they see as more important. And either way, Heller will absolutely NOT be good inspiration for all or most Lunars (hell, for basically 0 published Lunars so far), just like Dracula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T14:00:12-08:00","id":347659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. &quot;What he looks like&quot; vs. &quot;almost everything else about him&quot;. What's more important?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no objectively-correct answer to this question. It completely depends on what you want to do with the character. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T14:42:20-08:00","id":347713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, the character I described is a Lunar character</div> </div> </div> </div>OK but, honestly, so what?<br /> <br /> You can do what you want to do, and that's great. Others don't necessarily agree, but that's irrelevant.<br /> <br /> The great last stand for the honor of Prototype just seems like a lot of noise over nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T15:41:50-08:00","id":347791,"title":"","content":"Is Rater assuming that being a Liminal instead of a Lunar would be a bad thing, somehow? Like, it's objectively worse to be or play a Liminal?<br /> <br /> Like, we're somehow insulting Prototype by calling it Liminal material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-22-2014, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:24:01-08:00","id":347831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm assuming that 60% of Mercer and 80% of Heller can't be modled with Liminals, which means that 75% of the traits possessed by the MAin Characters of the Prototype Franchise are Lunaresque traits, not Infernal traits or Abyssal Traits or Liminal Traits.<br /> <br /> What great stand?I'm just saying that if I want to make a character inspired by James Heller, I have to us a Lunar and give up the &quot;Bio-Horror&quot; aesthetic because if I play a Liminal and keep that Aesthetic, I have to give up ...everything else that's important to the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, are you making massive assumptions about how the powers of a brand-new, never-before-seen splat will work in a year or whatever when that book comes out, and worrying (with a straight face) that those as-yet-unrevealed mechanics won't support your concept?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:33:19-08:00","id":347840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. At no point did I say anything about being inspiration for <b>all</b> Lunars. I said I saw elements that can be used to make a Lunar character, and that their are more Lunar Elements than most are willing to admit. To say otherwise tells me that either you're not reading my words carefully or that you're trying to make me out as a straw man.<br /> <br /> 2. &amp;quot;What he looks like&amp;quot; vs. &amp;quot;almost everything else about him&amp;quot;. What's more important?</div> </div> </div> </div>In point of fact, by responding to developer statements that Prototype is not good inspiration for Lunars, number 1 is EXACTLY what you are saying, or else you are (as several folks have pointed out) saying NOTHING. <br /> <br /> Because no one outside of your own imagination has argued that Heller, divorced of aesthetics, cannot serve as inspiration for A Lunar. They've said that Prototype (as a whole, aesthetics included but not exclusively) is not good inspiration for Lunars generally, and some have suggested it may be better inspiration for Liminals generally. <br /> <br /> If you are NOT arguing against this latter portion, then you're not arguing anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:33:52-08:00","id":347842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm assuming that 60% of Mercer and 80% of Heller can't be modled with Liminals, which means that 75% of the traits possessed by the MAin Characters of the Prototype Franchise are Lunaresque traits, not Infernal traits or Abyssal Traits or Liminal Traits.<br /> <br /> What great stand?I'm just saying that if I want to make a character inspired by James Heller, I have to us a Lunar and give up the &quot;Bio-Horror&quot; aesthetic because if I play a Liminal and keep that Aesthetic, I have to give up ...everything else that's important to the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition I would completely agree, but only because second edition Lunars don't have a clear theme or narrative or whatever. I'll be honest by saying that Prototype struck me as inspirational material for <i>charms</i> and <i>stunts</i> of Lunar characters, but not for general character story, themes and visuals. Bayonetta would fit the Lunar themes much better than Mercer, but that's not the point.<br /> <br /> In third edition, Lunars have been described as <i>bestial</i>, <i>barbaric</i> and <i>physical</i>. Mercer and Heller fit only on the Physical scale (and shapeshifting). That's why we're saying that Lunar is not a good fit for Mercer <i>as is</i>.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, any character can fit any charm or power. Every Solar/Dragon-blooded/Lunar/Sidereal/Liminal/Infernal/Abyssal/God-Blooded can jump 10 times higher than normal and destroy the gound on impact. They can all hit so hard his target simply explodes. The real difference lies in <i>narrative</i>, <i>themes</i> and <i>visuals</i>.<br /> <br /> Can you play a Lunar with the <i>powers</i> from Mercer or Heller? Change the visual slightly and you're done. We're not telling you this is wrong. We're telling you that if you would want to take these two protagonists intact, without any modification in their style and place them in the Exalted world, they would fit the Liminal/Abyssal narrative much better than that of the Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T16:36:40-08:00","id":347846,"title":"","content":"See I think Rater was making this case that dudes from Prototype can be inspirations for his Lunars, which is totally cool.<br /> <br /> The reason everyone is angry that he's arguing the point over and over... is because everyone else was arguing with him. Now that his thesis is made more clearly, everyone appears to agree with him, but it's still an arguing kind of agreement.<br /> <br /> The argument is over, the thread is won! But... at what cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T19:53:00-08:00","id":347949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> My point is that Protptype can be taken as inspiration for <b>A </b>lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, then, as I said, you're essentially arguing nothing. At least insofar as no one disagrees with you to my knowledge. And Kunoichi's statement notwithstanding, I'm not convinced anyone ever has disagreed with this statement in this thread. I know several folks have specifically agreed with it, and Isator Levi made the &quot;A Lunar vs ALL Lunars inspiration&quot; point pages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:38:14-08:00","id":348122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y<br /> I'm essentially contesting the &quot;Lunars aren't Prototype&quot; statement ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is preciely why the discussion is confused. You're take a generalist statement about presentation and themes of Lunars as a whole group, and trying to contest it with reference to a single case while discounting any discussion of themes and aesthetics out of hand. <br /> <br /> The statement you're contesting has it's mind on the guiding themes of Lunars as a whole, without any reference to their implementation. Lunars 'aren't prototype' in the same way as they 'aren't vampires' or 'aren't Teen Wolf'. How that's done mechnically and where it overlaps with other tropes in other works (such as superhuman resilience, in just about everything, or revenge plots, in just about everything else') is neither here nor there. <br /> <br /> A lot of the things that you've said are perfectly true an there's nothing stopping you from making the character you want to ... but that's really besides the point of the statement you seem to be tilting at.<br /> <br /> It's as though someone came out and said 'Solars are glorious heroes', and you replied by saying 'But I can make Lyta, a genocidial mad-woman determined to burn all of the Dragon-blooded alive!' Both of these things can be true without contradicting one another.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:29:34-08:00","id":348222,"title":"","content":"Hm. Okay, got linked here, haven't read anything past the first post, might as well post my two cents.<br /> <br /> Prototype provides some really good <i>incentives</i> for playing a Lunar. If you're a new player, and you come to me and say &quot;I want to do the stuff Alex Mercer does&quot;, I will point you toward Lunars, because they offer easy access to what is essentially the full package. You want to turn your hands into rending claws, you want to kill someone and take their shape, you want to eat someone's brain to take their memories, you want to regenerate from dreadful wounds, you want to leap over walls and sprint up buildings, that's all easily available to Lunars.<br /> <br /> Where Lunar power - Lunar transformation - fundamentally differs from that of Alex Mercer is in its <i>attitude</i>.<br /> <br /> Now, pretty much every Exalt has &quot;transformation&quot; available to them as a basic thing, just by virtue of their anima - Henshin A Go Go, Baby - but the splats that really focus on it as part of their powers are Lunars, Infernals and Abyssals. I'm keeping transformation distinct from &quot;disguise&quot; here - I mean in terms of a drastic alteration of the self. Setting aside the mechanical specifics, the difference is in their attitude toward transformation.<br /> <br /> Abyssals approach transformation in the sense of a Gothic revelation. Rather than a true change, the edifice of normality decays to reveal the horror that always lurked beneath.<br /> Infernals approach transformation in the sense of body horror. The changes are unnatural, alien distortions and extrusions. Bodyparts swell and wither, skin tears under dreadful pressure.<br /> Lunars approach transformation in the sense of shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> This is the forms taken by Greek gods in Homer, which are often phrased ambiguously enough that they could be analogies or literal changes or both. It's the enchanted skins of Norse myth, that allowed gods and dwarfs to take on the shapes of animals as easily as donning a cloak. It's the transfigurations of youkai, living illusions whose changes are as much fancy as reality.<br /> <br /> The Lunar attitude to transformation does not involve strict biology - it's not the horrifying, painful change you see in Werewolf in New York, or the disgusting process of Animorphing. It doesn't involve unrecognizable or purely alien changes - it's not the mad one-winged angel forms of final bosses, or the grotesque mutations of Resident Evil bosses. It's more fae than that - <i>supernatural</i>, but not <i>unnatural</i>. Even at their least plausible, Lunar transformations involve exaggerated or chimeric forms - a housecat dancing over empty space with eyes burning bright and witchlight dancing between its two tails, or a vast eagle with the head of a dog and leonine paws bellowing loud enough to shatter towers - rather than alien ones.<br /> <br /> So in terms of specific aesthetics, Prototype isn't great for Lunars, because even if the practical capabilities it offers are the same, its attitude is one of body horror - you are literally playing a Resident Evil boss (who becomes another, less interesting Resident Evil boss in the next game) - rather than &quot;shapeshifting&quot; in the sense that Lunars undertake it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:05:30-08:00","id":348251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Revlid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/342244-prototype-as-lunar-inspiration?p=348222#post348222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar attitude to transformation does not involve strict biology... <b>It's more fae than that</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I already used my allocation of posting the &quot;NOOOOOOO!&quot; video from The Office. &quot;Fae&quot; isn't the term to use when it's been shown to work like the reason that cWoD Imbued called werewolves &quot;flickers&quot;. One moment, a human is standing there. The next? A monster or a beast is before you, and there''s blood on his face, my god there's blood etc. etc. No need at all to relate it to Fair Folk. Let's keep away from that around here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:29:42-08:00","id":348292,"title":"","content":"Might I ask who linked you here, Rev?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:40:18-08:00","id":348312,"title":"","content":"Wasn't me, glad as I am to see him here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}